{"name":"Angel in Blue Jeans","hex":"#bbc6d9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An incorporeal and holy or semidivine messenger from a deity or other divine entity, traditionally depicted as a youthful, winged figure in flowing robes.\n\n One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues.","One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To support by donating money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"jeans","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pair of trousers made from denim cotton."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of jean"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jeans"}],"entries":[{"title":"Angel in Blue Jeans","blocks":[{"text":"\"Angel in Blue Jeans\" is a song recorded by American rock band Train for their seventh studio album Bulletproof Picasso. The song was written by Pat Monahan, Amund Bjørklund, and Espen Lind, and was produced by the latter two as well as Butch Walker. It was released on June 9, 2014 as the lead single from the album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Angelinbluejeanstrain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_in_Blue_Jeans","wikidata":"Q17620559"},{"title":"Jeans","blocks":[{"text":"Jeans are a type of trousers made from denim or dungaree cloth. Often the term \"jeans\" refers to a particular style of trousers, called \"blue jeans\", with the addition of copper pocket rivets added by Jacob W. Davis in 1871 and patented by Davis and Levi Strauss on May 20, 1873. Prior to the patent, the term \"blue jeans\" had been long in use for various items of workwear, constructed from a heavy blue-colored denim fabric."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Jeans.jpg/330px-Jeans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeans","wikidata":"Q83363"},{"title":"Angel in Blue","blocks":[{"text":"\"Angel in Blue\" is a song written by Seth Justman that was first released by the J. Geils Band on their 1981 album Freeze Frame. Cissy Houston and Luther Vandross appear on the song as back up vocalists.\n\"Angel in Blue\" was also released on a number of J. Geils Band compilation albums, including Centerfold, The Very Best J. Geils Band Album Ever and Best of The J. Geils Band, as well as several multi-artist compilation albums."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/Angel_in_Blue_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_in_Blue","wikidata":"Q4762314"},{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of God. In Western belief-systems the term is often used to distinguish benevolent from malevolent intermediary beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/330px-Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel","wikidata":"Q235113"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Blue_jeans_fading.png/500px-Blue_jeans_fading.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Blue_jeans_fading.png/1280px-Blue_jeans_fading.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Blue_jeans_fading.png/500px-Blue_jeans_fading.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Microscopic image of faded fabric","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_jeans_fading.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Manifattura_genovese%2C_abito_da_festa_in_tela_di_genova_%28jeans%29%2C_1850-1900_ca..JPG/500px-Manifattura_genovese%2C_abito_da_festa_in_tela_di_genova_%28jeans%29%2C_1850-1900_ca..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Manifattura_genovese%2C_abito_da_festa_in_tela_di_genova_%28jeans%29%2C_1850-1900_ca..JPG/1280px-Manifattura_genovese%2C_abito_da_festa_in_tela_di_genova_%28jeans%29%2C_1850-1900_ca..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Manifattura_genovese%2C_abito_da_festa_in_tela_di_genova_%28jeans%29%2C_1850-1900_ca..JPG/500px-Manifattura_genovese%2C_abito_da_festa_in_tela_di_genova_%28jeans%29%2C_1850-1900_ca..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A traditional women's Genoese dress in \"blue jeans\" (1890s). Palazzo Spinola di Pellicceria, Genoa, Italy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManifattura_genovese%2C_abito_da_festa_in_tela_di_genova_(jeans)%2C_1850-1900_ca..JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons